# VTID-03774 — commands run during investigation and verification

## Investigation (read-only, live tracing)

User reported: "when I select a session, it now starts immediately with a
new day greeting, no guided topic content at all" — right after VTID-03771
shipped and was confirmed deployed to staging.

Self-allocated VTID via Supabase RPC:
  SELECT allocate_global_vtid('claude-code', 'gateway', 'orb-live-guided-topic');
  -> VTID-03774

Queried recent oasis_events for the real account (bc34a5ca-...):
  SELECT created_at, topic, message, left(metadata::text, 700) AS meta
  FROM oasis_events
  WHERE metadata->>'user_id' = 'bc34a5ca-6966-44f6-9507-3bed98e3e1d5'
    AND created_at BETWEEN '2026-08-27 11:59:05' AND '2026-08-27 11:59:41'
  ORDER BY created_at ASC;

Found two client sessions: live-d1894cf2... (won guided-topic T003, played
412 audio chunks / ~29s of real narration, turn_count reached 1) then
live-2313a2e1... (superseded the first after a "connection" disconnect,
ambient candidates all skipped, unread_messages_announce won instead).

Initially misread `orb.livekit.next_action.suppressed`'s
`suppress_reason:"all_sources_skipped"` as covering the WHOLE wake-brief
decision. Corrected this by finding the real emitter:
  grep -rn "next_action.suppressed\|all_sources_skipped" services --include=*.ts
-> confirmed via services/assistant-continuation/telemetry.ts and an earlier
changelog entry (2026-08-16 row) that `orb.livekit.next_action.*` is a
legacy-named SHARED wake-brief telemetry prefix, but the *suppressed* event
specifically covers only the Contextual Next Action provider's own 8
ambient sub-sources — NOT the overall winning candidate across ALL
providers (guided-topic-narration, Teacher, journey-guide, etc).

Found the REAL per-session wake-brief decision record lives in
`orb_wake_timelines` (services/gateway/src/services/wake-timeline/wake-timeline-recorder.ts),
not oasis_events:
  SELECT session_id, transport, started_at, ended_at, aggregates, events
  FROM orb_wake_timelines
  WHERE session_id IN ('live-d1894cf2-cee9-45c8-b381-14bbfda20eb3',
                        'live-2313a2e1-c165-4768-94e3-f62e4f4734a6');

This returned session 2's full `continuation_decision_finished.providerResults`,
which shows definitively:
  {"key":"guided_topic_narration","reason":"no_topic_tapped","status":"skipped","latencyMs":1}
-> proof positive `guided_topic_id` never reached the server on this
   reconnect's start payload.

## Client-side investigation (orb-widget.js)

Confirmed vitana-v1 loads the SAME orb-widget.js as the Command Hub (not a
separate client):
  grep -rn "orb-widget\.js\|VitanaOrb\b" /home/user/vitana-v1/src --include=*.ts --include=*.tsx -l

Read _attemptReconnect(), _resetAndReconnect(), _sessionStart(), _hide(),
_endGuidedTopicTeaching(), focusGuidedTopic(), the turn-complete handler at
~line 2546, and the SSE es.onerror handler in full. Confirmed via grep that
the ONLY places `_s.guidedTopic`/`_s._guidedTopicInFlight` are assigned are:
  grep -n "_s.guidedTopic\s*=\|guidedAutoClose\s*=\s*false\|_guidedTopicInFlight" orb-widget.js
-> focusGuidedTopic (arm), turn-complete handler (clears guidedTopic only,
   NOT guidedTopicInFlight, by design), _hide() (clears both — real close),
   _attemptReconnect/_resetAndReconnect (restore-guards, both present and
   correctly ordered before _sessionStart() on static reading).

Fetched the LIVE deployed widget from staging to rule out a stale/uncached
build:
  curl -s "https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com/command-hub/orb-widget.js" -o /tmp/live-orb-widget.js
  diff /tmp/live-orb-widget.js services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
-> identical, confirms VTID-03770's fix genuinely live.

Computed RECONNECT_DELAYS[0]=1500ms and cross-checked against the observed
~33.0s disconnect -> ~36.9s reconnect timing — consistent with
_attemptReconnect()'s own scheduled retry (not the 5s health-probe
watchdog, which would fire later, at ~38.0s).

Noticed `session_start_received.reconnectStage:"idle"` on the SECOND
session, which is inconsistent with `_s._preDisconnectStage` having been
set to "speaking" by _announceDisconnect() (narration audio was actively
playing at disconnect time) — a genuine anomaly, but chasing it further
(would `_s.audioPlaying` even be true during Polly-bridge playback vs a
live model turn?) did not converge on a conclusive explanation and is
flagged as unresolved in acceptance.md rather than guessed at.

Exhaustively checked and RULED OUT:
  - A race between _attemptReconnect's scheduled retry and the 5s
    health-probe watchdog calling _resetAndReconnect concurrently (timing
    doesn't support the watchdog having fired yet).
  - _endGuidedTopicTeaching() clearing state via a premature model tool-call
    (would have called _hide(), which would have closed the overlay
    entirely — inconsistent with the overlay staying open and a new
    session opening with real audio).
  - orb.destroy()/orb.init() via useOrbVoiceWidget.ts's auth-change reinit
    effect or unmount cleanup (module-scoped `_s` is never reallocated by
    either; _s.guidedTopic/_guidedTopicInFlight would survive a
    destroy+reinit cycle even if one occurred).
  - orb.updateContext() clobbering guidedTopic (vitana-v1's route-change
    effect never sends `guided_topic_id` in its updateContext payload).

Could not conclusively identify the exact caller/ordering bug from static
analysis + oasis_events/orb_wake_timelines alone — no live-browser console
access from this session (same standing environment limitation as
VTID-03763). Documented as an open item in acceptance.md rather than
claimed fixed.

## Server-side investigation (live-session-controller.ts)

Read wake-brief-wiring.ts in full (decideWakeBriefForSession): confirmed
`guidedTopicId` is forwarded regardless of isReconnect, and
guided-topic-narration gets a 10s provider timeout on any explicit
selection (EXPLICIT_SELECTION_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS) — ruling out a timeout
explanation for the missing candidate.

Read guided-topic-narration.ts's produce() in full: confirmed (per its own
VTID-03677 comment) it no longer reads isReconnect at all — returns a
candidate purely on topicId presence.

Read live-session-controller.ts around the wake-brief decision call site
(~line 1690-1760) and found a SEPARATE, independent defect: the injection
of `session.wakeBriefOverrideBlock` was gated unconditionally on
`!isReconnectStart`, with no exemption for a guided-topic winner — unlike
orb-live.ts (WS transport), which already carries this exact exemption via
`_hasPendingGuidedTopicAtOpen` (VTID-03727/VTID-03771):
  grep -n "isReconnectStart\|_hasPendingGuidedTopicAtOpen" routes/orb-live.ts

This is a real, independent bug (defense-in-depth fix, not proven to be
THIS incident's specific cause, since guided_topic_narration never even
competed here per the `no_topic_tapped` evidence) — but would matter in a
future case where guided_topic_id DOES reach the server on a reconnect.

## Implementation

### Fix 1 — services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js

Inside `_sessionStart()`, immediately before
`startPayload.guided_topic_id = _s.guidedTopic;`:
  - Added a restore-fallback: `if (!_s.guidedTopic && _s._guidedTopicInFlight) { ... _s.guidedTopic = _s._guidedTopicInFlight; }`
  - Added diagnostic console.log of guidedTopic/guidedTopicInFlight/
    preDisconnectStage/isReconnectAttempt on every _sessionStart() call.

### Fix 2 — services/gateway/src/orb/live/session/live-session-controller.ts

  - Added `export function shouldInjectWakeBriefOverrideBlock(isReconnectStart, dedupeKey)`
    above buildVertexWakeBriefBlock — pure predicate, returns
    `!isReconnectStart || dedupeKey?.startsWith('guided_topic:')`.
  - Updated the call site to use it:
    `if (picked && line && line.length > 0 && shouldInjectWakeBriefOverrideBlock(isReconnectStart, picked.dedupeKey)) {`

