### Mutation testing — Fix 1 (widget)

Backed up orb-widget.js, removed exactly the new
`if (!_s.guidedTopic && _s._guidedTopicInFlight) { ... }` block via a
python exact-match string-replace, re-ran the target test file: 3 of 18
tests failed (existence, no-op-when-set, log-presence — all 3 tied
directly to the removed block), the other 15 (including the unrelated
diagnostic-log test, which asserts a DIFFERENT log line the mutation
didn't touch) still passed. Restored the backup, re-verified
`node --check` clean.

### Mutation testing — Fix 2 (server predicate)

Two separate mutations, both restored after:
  1. Reverted the CALL SITE back to the old inline
     `!isReconnectStart` expression (bypassing the new predicate entirely)
     — the 5 new predicate unit tests still passed unchanged (expected:
     they call the exported function directly, not through the call site,
     so this mutation only proves the call site isn't accidentally
     duplicating logic — it does not exercise the call site itself, which
     has no integration test given the size of the surrounding pipeline).
  2. Reverted the PREDICATE's own body to `return !isReconnectStart;`
     (dropping the guided-topic exemption) — exactly 1 of 5 tests failed
     ("still injects on a reconnect when the winning candidate is a
     guided-topic resume"), the other 4 passed unaffected.
  Restored both mutations; re-verified `tsc --noEmit` clean and diff
  against backup was empty.

## Fix 3 — Codex review follow-up (post-review, same PR)

Codex bot (`chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`) left a P1 review comment on
`live-session-controller.ts:1820`: "Avoid restarting guided lessons on
reconnect." Read it carefully and verified it independently before acting:

  - Confirmed `guidedTopicAudioDelivered` (routes/orb-live.ts,
    `sendGuidedTopicNarrationAudioBridge`) is a per-SESSION-OBJECT flag,
    and a reconnect always creates a brand new session object — so its
    "including reconnects" doc comment claim is false; it cannot prevent a
    replay across a reconnect. Read the full function (lines 10840-10894).
  - Confirmed `guidedTopicNarrationContent` bundling
    (live-session-controller.ts ~1879-1889) is driven purely by the
    candidate WINNING, independent of the `shouldInjectWakeBriefOverrideBlock`
    gate Fix 2 touches — meaning the replay risk applies broadly to Fix 1
    (the client resending guided_topic_id more reliably), not narrowly to
    Fix 2's own gate.
  - Confirmed `ws-start-adapter.ts:141` calls the exact same
    `handleLiveSessionStart` this file exports — `live-session-controller.ts`
    is shared session-start infrastructure for BOTH WS and SSE, not
    SSE-only as this PR's own body originally claimed (corrected in
    acceptance.md rather than silently left wrong).
  - Confirmed `userFacingLine` empty string is a valid candidate shape:
      grep -n "userFacingLine" services/assistant-continuation/types.ts
    -> only `typeof c.userFacingLine !== 'string'` fails validation; an
       empty string still passes for ANY candidate kind, not only the
       special `none_with_reason` sentinel the doc comment focuses on.

Implemented the isResume mechanism described in acceptance.md's "Fix 3"
section:
  - orb-widget.js: new `_guidedTopicAudioDelivered` flag (declared near
    `_guidedTopicInFlight`), reset false in `focusGuidedTopic()`, flipped
    true in the turn-complete handler at the exact point that already
    nulls `_s.guidedTopic`, cleared in `_hide()`. `_sessionStart()` sends
    `startPayload.guided_topic_resume = true` nested inside the existing
    `if (_s.guidedTopic) { startPayload.guided_topic_id = ... }` block.
  - routes/orb-live.ts: added `guided_topic_resume?: boolean;` to the
    `GeminiLiveSession` interface (required by tsc once the session-creation
    object literal in live-session-controller.ts set the field).
  - orb/live/session/live-session-controller.ts: reads
    `body.guided_topic_resume` onto the session object (defensive:
    `=== true`, so a non-boolean/malformed value silently resolves to
    `false`), forwards `guidedTopicResume` into `decideWakeBriefForSession`.
  - services/wake-brief-wiring.ts: added `guidedTopicResume?: boolean` to
    `DecideWakeBriefArgs`, forwarded into
    `extra[GUIDED_TOPIC_NARRATION_EXTRA_KEY]` as `isResume`.
  - services/assistant-continuation/providers/guided-topic-narration.ts:
    added `isResume?: boolean` to the inputs type + `readInputs()`; in
    `produce()`, skip the Polly synthesis call when `isResume` (narrationAudio
    stays null) and compute `spokenLesson` as `''` instead of the opener/
    post-narration line. The candidate still returns and still wins
    (unchanged priority/dedupeKey/guidedTopicNarration bundling) — only the
    spoken line and audio are suppressed.

